 "narrative": [
  "Admission into the Political Science major is contingent upon successful completion of the requirements stipulated below.\nOnce the pre-major is completed with a 2.6 UC GPA or higher, students may petition for admission into full major status. Admission to the pre-major does not guarantee admission to full major status.\nTo qualify for admission into full major status, students must complete three courses from Political Science 1, 6, 7, and 12, as well as Political Science 15, with a UC grade-point average of 2.6 or above. In addition, students must complete Economics 1 and 2 (or 9) on a letter graded basis. Economics 1 and 2 (or 9) are excluded from the pre-major grade-point average computation but are included in the overall major GPA.\nTransfer and upper-division students should consult the undergraduate advisor about course substitutions."
